## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to add data quality at streaming scale with per-tenant isolation and governance.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming validation with Great Expectations in Dataflow
- Per-tenant BigQuery partitions and access controls
- DLQ handling, metrics, and rollback tests
- Schema evolution and retention policies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Dataflow DoFn for validation using GE-like rules
class ValidateFn extends DoFn {
  processElement(ctx){
    const rec=ctx.element;
    if(!valid(rec)){ ctx.output(badTag, rec); } else { ctx.output(goodTag, rec); }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test validating rules with synthetic tenants?
- How would you monitor prod quality drift across tenants and trigger rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical observability and data reliability skills in a real-world, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Beam Metrics and Cloud Monitoring integration
- Idempotent streaming writes with insertId
- Lightweight auditing and error handling
- Alerting on data quality metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-beam sketch (JavaScript/TypeScript syntax used for illustration)
class ParseEvent extends DoFn {
  @ProcessElement
  process(@Element json, output) {
    const event = JSON.parse(json.image);
    this.ingested.inc();
    // ... validation and transformation
    this.processed.inc();
    output(event);
  }

  @Setup
  setup() {
    this.ingested = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'ingested_events');
    this.processed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'processed_events');
    this.failed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'failed_events');
  }
}
```
